From: Akshay Kakatkar <me@kakatkarakshay.dev>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: select valid link when link zero is missing

The TX control link field can contain zero for MLD frames even when link
zero is not part of the VIF. ath12k treats that value as an explicit link,
fails to find an arvif and drops the frame.

Select the first driver-backed active link when the VIF does not have link
zero. The existing TX link selection can still apply STA-specific policy.

Intersect active_links with links_map so that this does not redirect frames
to links which are being removed. If no active driver link remains, retain
the existing teardown behavior and drop the frame.

Fixes: 648a121bafa3 ("wifi: ath12k: ath12k_mac_op_tx(): MLO support")
Signed-off-by: Akshay Kakatkar <me@kakatkarakshay.dev>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
@@ -938,6 +938,11 @@ static void ath12k_wifi7_mac_op_tx(struc
 
 	/* handle only for MLO case, use deflink for non MLO case */
 	if (ieee80211_vif_is_mld(vif)) {
+		links_map = vif->active_links & ahvif->links_map;
+		if (link_id == ATH12K_DEFAULT_LINK_ID &&
+		    !(vif->valid_links & BIT(link_id)) && links_map)
+			link_id = __ffs(links_map);
+
 		link_id = ath12k_mac_get_tx_link(sta, vif, link_id, skb, info_flags);
 		if (link_id >= IEEE80211_MLD_MAX_NUM_LINKS) {
 			ieee80211_free_txskb(hw, skb);
